# .env is intentionally NOT excluded here — EAS Build's remote workers need
# it to inline @env values via babel-plugin-react-native-dotenv, the same
# way `expo start --dev-client` already does from local disk. Excluding it
# silently produced a release bundle with every @env value (including all
# Firebase config) resolved to undefined, since babel.config.js allows
# undefined env vars rather than failing the build.

